  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 937 PM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nWednesday night the cut off low will finally shift eastward as a\ntrough axis moves into the Midwest and skies will become partly \ncloudy across the TN Valley. Will see a low chance (20-30%) of\nshowers and thunderstorms mainly east of I-65 Thursday afternoon.\nA little bit higher rain chances on Friday afternoon as the trough \naxis makes it into the OH Valley and sends a disturbance into the TN\nValley. The sfc low lifts into the Lower Great Lakes while the \nassociated cold front will not make much southern progress, remaining\nup in the OH Valley. Not much of a pattern change over the weekend\nas it looks like the front will not make it into the region and we\nwill continue to get diurnally driven showers and thunderstorms. \n\nTemps will be in the upper 80s to lower 90s Thursday through \nSunday but the heat index will make it feel more like it is in the\nupper 90s to just above 100 degrees. Not reaching heat advisory \nthresholds, however with most of us returning back to school this \nweek, heat safety needs to remain a priority.",
